Package: RTutorRDDisclosure
Type: Package
Title: RTutor Problem Set on Voluntary R&D Disclosure under Asymmetric Information
Version: 0.1
Date: 2026-24-09
Author: Niklas Lieb
Maintainer: Niklas Lieb <niklasue@gmx.de>
Description: Interactive RTutor problem set, written as a bachelor's thesis at
    Ulm University, that replicates and explains the empirical analysis of
    Baruffaldi, Simeth, and Wehrheim (2024, Management Science). Users study
    whether research-intensive firms publish more scientific articles after
    brokerage house mergers and closures reduce their analyst coverage. The
    problem set covers omitted variable bias, a difference-in-differences
    design with firm, year, and event fixed effects, an event study of
    pre-trends, a matching estimator, and heterogeneity analyses by
    information asymmetry, financial constraints, and proprietary costs.
License: Not yet licensed by the author. The default suggestion for licensing is
	Problem set content: Creative Commons (CC BY-SA)
	Package code: GPL >= 2.0
Depends: RTutor, haven, dplyr, skimr, ggplot2, dagitty, ggdag, lfe, stargazer
